---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brands, categories } from '../lib/catalog.js';
---
<Base
  title="About CouponsAndDeals — How We Work & How We Make Money"
  description="What CouponsAndDeals is, how offers are sourced and verified, and how affiliate links fund the site."
  canonical="/about"
>
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px;padding:2rem 1.1rem">
    <h1>About CouponsAndDeals</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      CouponsAndDeals lists coupon codes and deals from {brands.length} US stores across
      {categories.length} categories. Offers are pulled automatically from the
      affiliate networks each store partners with, refreshed several times a day,
      and expired codes are removed on every sync.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      When you click a coupon or deal on this site and make a purchase, we may earn
      a commission from the store through affiliate networks such as Impact,
      Commission Junction, Awin, and Rakuten. This is how the site is funded. It
      never changes the price you pay, and it doesn't influence which offers we
      show — offers come from the stores' own published promotions.
    </p>
    <p>
      As an Amazon Associate, CouponsAndDeals earns from qualifying purchases.
    </p>

    <h2>How offers are verified</h2>
    <p>
      Offers come directly from each store's affiliate program feed — the same
      promotions the store publishes itself — rather than user submissions, so
      codes are valid when listed. Expiry dates are honored automatically: an
      expired offer is dropped from the site at the next rebuild.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, corrections, or store removal requests:
      <a href="mailto:contact@example.com">contact@example.com</a>.
      <!-- TODO: replace with your real contact address before applying to networks -->
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
